[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T20:29:22-07:00","id":1064631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1064229-iron-fist-as-a-mage?p=1064545#post1064545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also think, given his origin, that Wu Lung would be a more likely tradition for him to be associated with than the Akashic Brotherhood.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not really? He's white so that cancels any Wu Lung option there, but also their paradigm is ritualistic based, yes there are tiger warrior members but martial arts and Meditation is nto basically their sole instrament. The Wu Lung are not Monastic that's very much the opposite of their Paradigm.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-19T18:50:03-07:00","id":1065045,"title":"","content":"I was thinking in terms of the otherdimensional city where they're headquartered and the association with dragons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-19T19:20:38-07:00","id":1065055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1064229-iron-fist-as-a-mage?p=1065045#post1065045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking in terms of the otherdimensional city where they're headquartered and the association with dragons.</div> </div> </div> </div>AKashics also use the Dragon symbol and had Horizon Realms/Chantries.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'd say Gao is alot closer to Wu Lung.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2715,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","user":"Lian","date":". 03-20-2017, 04:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T06:31:31-07:00","id":1065714,"title":"","content":"I'm a few episodes in and I still haven't seen anything that couldn't be accomplished with Prime or Forces 2. I'm guessing the other powers show up later in the show. I really liked the Immortal Iron Fist comic and kinda wish they make something like that as a live action thing some day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T09:53:21-07:00","id":1065829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1064229-iron-fist-as-a-mage?p=1065714#post1065714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a few episodes in and I still haven't seen anything that couldn't be accomplished with Prime or Forces 2. I'm guessing the other powers show up later in the show. I really liked the Immortal Iron Fist comic and kinda wish they make something like that as a live action thing some day.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well ther's stuff he needs life 3 for by episode 4 and by the end of the series.<br /> <br /> I'd honestly say he He makes a better Shih though<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T14:26:29-07:00","id":1065943,"title":"","content":"In my opinion, the comic book version of Danny and the other Iron fists do seem to eventually hit mage level capabilities in terms of power and flexibility.<br /> <br /> Danny seems to have:<br /> Life 3 (Superhuman physical prowess, Heal self and others, Recover from cancer, Resist Zombie plague)<br /> Forces 2 (&quot;The Iron Fist&quot;, weird stuff like amplifying his magnetic properties to fly towards at train at high speed on a maglev track, surviving explosions)<br /> Mind 2 (Control of own mind, Some degree of resistance to mental powers, Some influence on human thoughts and emotions, Some telepathic ability... and sensing auras)<br /> <br /> But with the whole dragon thing, and the way it seems to work, I'd build Shou-Lao and the Iron Fist as some sort of powerful living wonder<br /> <br /> So if we're using mage, I'd suggest he began his superhero career as some sort of mystic martial artist with additional powers granted by Shou-Lao and through continued use of such powers awakened as a mage, probably some time after the Heroes for Hire was formed.<br /> <br /> (Edit: Or maybe Shou-Lao is some sort of Awaken or die sort of test)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 03-21-2017, 10:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}